 kit delivery - lists the artifacts, environments, and deployments the forge holds

   one of
   *kit delivery*  lists the artifacts, environments, and deployments the forge holds

     --text   --json   --jq
                           prints the stages as text, even on a terminal

   --stages      prints the stages, one per line, in order, the same over any workspace
   --marks       prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what the stage
                 draws does: for each, the forge's own mark of its runs, as a run makes each
   artifacts     {id, name, digest, size, run, age, expires}, keyed by its id: digest is the
                 forge's, as sha256:…, null on GitLab and Azure DevOps, which show none; size in
                 bytes; run the run that kept it; age seconds since it was made; expires when it
                 goes, in seconds since the epoch, or null. The name links to its page. GitHub reads
                 its 100 newest, GitLab the archives of its 100 newest successful jobs, Azure DevOps
                 those of its 20 newest runs; where there are more, the document is limited, at how
                 many it drew
   environments  {name, protection, approvers, branches}, keyed by its name: protection the kinds of
                 rule that guard it, as reviewers, wait, branches, or deployers; approvers who may
                 approve, by login; branches those that may deploy there, a tag's as refs/tags/…,
                 null for any. GitLab names no branches, and a GitLab whose tier, or caller, cannot
                 read protected environments leaves protection and approvers null. The name links to
                 its page. GitHub reads the branch policies of 20 environments that have their own,
                 and the list is limited before a 21st
   deployments   {id, environment, ref, sha, state, actor, age}, keyed by its id: state is success,
                 failure, running, waiting, cancelled, or inactive; actor who made it; age seconds
                 since. environment links to its row in environments, sha to the commit's page, and
                 state to its log. Azure DevOps reads the deployment records of the 20 environments
                 changed last, and names each one's ref, commit, and actor from its run among the
                 100 newest; where there are more, the document is limited, at how many it drew
   releases      a tab kit flow prints; on a terminal it opens in kittui, and with a form it is
                 refused
   builds        a tab kit flow prints; on a terminal it opens in kittui, and with a form it is
                 refused


 kit delivery
